On Mon, 16 Oct 2006, defklown wrote:

> I'm running Windows XP.
>
> I created a shortcut to NetHack.exe. I opened up the properties of the
> shortcut and changed the target field to read
> "C:\blahblahblah\nethack-343-win\Nethack.exe -D -uwizard". Windows gave
> me the "name not valid, make sure filepath is correct" error. How can I
> make this work?

The first part of the command line is the name of the executable. Because
of your ", the complete string is parsed as the first part. You need to
enclose only the part upto the .exe in quotes, the arguments stay
outside.

